(function(){"use strict";window.EDMUND_DSE_LISTENING_2013_TRANSCRIPT=Object.freeze({"partA":{"1":[{"start":0,"end":0.58,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task 1."},{"start":1.16,"end":7.28,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"The research team leader, Linda Lee, is interviewing a traveller in the airport departure hall."},{"start":8.1,"end":11.44,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"She has asked you to help fill in the interview form below."},{"start":12.72,"end":17.14,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Write the information in the spaces according to the traveller's answers."},{"start":18.34,"end":21.92,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"One space has been filled in for you as an example."},{"start":23.56,"end":26.48,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task."},{"start":27.5,"end":32.02,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"At the end of the task, you will have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":65.18,"end":71.06,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Excuse me, my name's Linda Lee and I work for the airport authority's research division."},{"start":71.86,"end":75.88,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"We're trying to find out what travellers think of the facilities here."},{"start":76.54,"end":78.56,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Would you mind if I asked you a few questions?"},{"start":78.56,"end":85,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Not at all. My flight's been delayed several hours, so I have all the time in the world."},{"start":85.9,"end":91.54,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"You look very smartly dressed. Am I right in thinking you're on a work-related trip?"},{"start":92.3,"end":94.62,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, thanks. But no, I'm not."},{"start":95.14,"end":103,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I usually dress smartly because it gives you a better chance of being upgraded to business or first class if the plane is overbooked."},{"start":103.46,"end":105.4,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Clever. I've never thought of that."},{"start":106.09,"end":109.21,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"So you're heading off for a nice holiday somewhere."},{"start":109.91,"end":117.55,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I wish I were. Unfortunately, my mother, she lives in the UK, has been taken ill, so I'm going home to see her."},{"start":118.09,"end":122.75,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Oh, I'm very sorry to hear that. So you know what to tick there, Chris?"},{"start":124.15,"end":129.97,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, I guess you've already answered my second question, which is about the length of your flight."},{"start":130.77,"end":133.63,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"London is quite a distance, isn't it?"},{"start":133.63,"end":140.11,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"He can say that again. Though I still think doing the trip in 13 hours is something of a miracle."},{"start":141.77,"end":145.61,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"And how often do you fly each year? Is it just once or twice?"},{"start":146.11,"end":154.97,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Oh, no. I fly way more than that. I have to do a lot of travelling for work, so I reckon probably about 10 to 12 trips a year."},{"start":155.65,"end":162.36,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Wow, up to a dozen trips a year? That's a lot. And do you fly to the UK often?"},{"start":162.36,"end":168.46,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Not really. This is the first time in years, actually. I can't bear the weather, you know."},{"start":169.02,"end":175.86,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I prefer Thailand for my holidays, so I fly to Bangkok several times a year. Bangkok's so close."},{"start":176.54,"end":184.78,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I also go to Singapore for business quite frequently. And as my daughter's studying in Australia, I fly to Sydney quite often."},{"start":185.42,"end":191.14,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Er, that's S-Y, not S-I. You spelt it wrong."},{"start":191.14,"end":196.58,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Oh, Chris, just copy it from the flight information up there."},{"start":198.33,"end":206.09,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Now, what do you most like about the environment of this airport? I mean, the layout, the design, that kind of thing."},{"start":206.47,"end":209.29,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, firstly, I really appreciate the daylight."},{"start":210.05,"end":210.25,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Daylight?"},{"start":210.83,"end":217.79,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Yes. So many airports are all closed in and gloomy. They make you feel like you're in a plane already."},{"start":217.79,"end":224.83,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"But all these windows, they make it seem as if you're outside. It's very thoughtful of the designers."},{"start":226.32,"end":229.34,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Another thing I like is that there's plenty of lounge space."},{"start":230.02,"end":232.32,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"What do you mean by lounge space?"},{"start":232.98,"end":239.24,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, take the seats we're sitting on in this lounge, for example. There's a big space between each row."},{"start":239.86,"end":246.98,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Some airports cram all the passengers together while they're waiting, so they're all hot and bothered before they even get on the plane."},{"start":246.98,"end":248.44,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"That's a good point."},{"start":249.46,"end":256.8,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"And a third thing I like is the moving walkways. Airports are getting bigger and bigger, but not all of them have moving walkways."},{"start":257.44,"end":261.94,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Sometimes you have to walk for miles to get to the boarding gate or the immigration desk."},{"start":262.34,"end":266.04,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I know what you mean. London airport is especially bad."},{"start":267.48,"end":273.88,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Let me ask you about the things you don't like now. What are the things that you think could be improved?"},{"start":274.7,"end":282.72,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, I have to say the shops are often overcrowded. There are plenty of them, but really not enough space to move around them comfortably."},{"start":283.64,"end":292.44,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Another thing is, there's no post office in the transit lounge. I've got a whole bunch of checks I need to send here and nowhere to post them."},{"start":292.92,"end":296.58,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"That's a nuisance. We'll have to do something about that."},{"start":297.1,"end":301.4,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Oh, and I suppose one more thing is the trolleys are too small."},{"start":302.2,"end":305.78,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"That's T-R-O-L-L-E-Y, Chris."},{"start":306.84,"end":310.84,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I don't mean the trolleys in the check-in hall. I mean the transit lounge ones."},{"start":311.81,"end":317.11,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"You'd better specify that, Chris. He means only the transit lounge trolleys."},{"start":318.74,"end":327.58,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Finally, what I'd like to do is ask you to compare Hong Kong with Singapore airport, which is one you say you go to quite often."},{"start":327.58,"end":334.2,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"So would you say Singapore airport is better, worse, or about the same as regards facilities?"},{"start":335.91,"end":343.55,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"I'm afraid I'd have to say I like Singapore airport more. Yeah, it still has the edge over everywhere else."},{"start":344.23,"end":348.03,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"And what is it that makes it superior to Hong Kong? Anything in particular?"},{"start":348.69,"end":357.79,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Well, for one thing it has more greenery. You know, potted palms, flowers. There's even a garden. Yeah, more greenery."},{"start":358.65,"end":359.59,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Right, more greenery."},{"start":360.55,"end":366.27,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"And another thing is it has a movie theatre. You know, a cinema where you can watch free movies."},{"start":366.81,"end":371.09,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"Wow, that's great. Well, thanks for taking the time to talk to us."},{"start":371.47,"end":371.89,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"My pleasure."},{"start":372.41,"end":376.31,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"And I hope you can find something to occupy yourself for the next few hours."},{"start":376.31,"end":382.97,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"In the meantime, put your business card in our lucky drawer hat. You could at least win some DVDs for yourself."},{"start":383.71,"end":388.27,"speaker":"Airport survey","text":"That's the end of task one. You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":451.47,"end":451.5,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task two. Linda is now interviewing another traveller about what facilities or features would be important in a new lounge area that is being planned at the airport."}],"2":[{"start":0,"end":11.17,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task two. Linda is now interviewing another traveller about what facilities or features would be important in a new lounge area that is being planned at the airport."},{"start":11.17,"end":20.23,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Listen to the traveller's answers and rank the facilities in order of how important she thinks they are."},{"start":21.11,"end":32.89,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Then note down her reasons. And finally, write the letter for the facility feature in the correct boxes one to six on page five."},{"start":32.89,"end":42.46,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have 30 seconds to study the task. At the end of the task, you'll have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":75.94,"end":82.66,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Excuse me, madam. My name's Linda Lee and I work for the airport authority. Are you waiting for the London flight?"},{"start":83.36,"end":88.42,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Yeah, it's been delayed and I have no idea how to fill the time."},{"start":88.86,"end":95.1,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, perhaps you could spare a few moments to look at this plan for a new lounge area which we're intending to build."},{"start":95.1,"end":108.3,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"We'd really appreciate your comments on it. We'll be including all the facilities and features on this list and would like you first of all to rank them in order of how important you think they are."},{"start":108.8,"end":110.66,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"OK, let's have a look at them."},{"start":111.48,"end":120.44,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Hmm. Well, I notice you have a coffee there. Would you say that a coffee shop was the most important thing to have in the lounge?"},{"start":120.44,"end":129,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, it certainly helps, especially when you have to wait all day for your plane. But I'd say it was of average importance, really."},{"start":129.54,"end":131.9,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"So you'd put it in the middle of the scale."},{"start":132.16,"end":141.7,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Sure. As far as I'm concerned, toilets are the main requirement. I always get nervous before a flight and need to, you know."},{"start":142.74,"end":146.06,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"So what do you think is the least important facility?"},{"start":146.76,"end":156.68,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"I guess it has to be the children's play area. No. Wait a minute. If you've got kids, I suppose you'd really appreciate something like that."},{"start":157.62,"end":166.72,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Let's say the internet corner. Yeah, the computer nerds meeting point. Well, you can tell I'm not an online sort of person."},{"start":167.38,"end":173.6,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"But you'd rate the children's play area as a better facility to have than a coffee shop, would you?"},{"start":173.6,"end":182.98,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Oh, no. I prefer coffee to kids. At least with a coffee, you can chuck it away if you don't like it. I'm only joking."},{"start":184.32,"end":190.88,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"So that leaves greenery as number two. I mean, plants. You rate that very highly, do you?"},{"start":191.34,"end":196.04,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Yes. Yes, I suppose I do. Do you have any particular reason for that?"},{"start":196.04,"end":204.66,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Yes. I think greenery, or plants, whatever you want to call it, adds color and freshness to a lounge."},{"start":205.32,"end":212.92,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"It adds color and freshness. Make a note of that, Chris. And what about toilets? Why did you put them at the top of your scale?"},{"start":213.5,"end":217.46,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Because the toilets on the plane are often cramped and smelly."},{"start":217.92,"end":224.74,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Not on every airline, surely. Most toilets on airplanes are cramped, but they're seldom smelly."},{"start":224.74,"end":229.04,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, I always travel cheap, so I don't expect the best."},{"start":229.84,"end":232.88,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Perhaps you shouldn't drink so much coffee before you get on."},{"start":233.54,"end":242.72,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Having coffee shops is a must, though. Everyone knows the coffee on planes tastes bad, and it's always lukewarm. You know, never hot enough."},{"start":243.3,"end":244.84,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"That's not always true."},{"start":244.96,"end":248.86,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"It is. Show me an airline where the coffee isn't rubbish."},{"start":248.86,"end":257.18,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"All right. Let's move on to the Internet corner, and let's try not to be rude about people who love computers."},{"start":258.26,"end":264.07,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, the reason I use computers is that most people use their own devices."},{"start":264.51,"end":268.01,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"You mean their own devices like smartphones and tablets?"},{"start":268.37,"end":272.39,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Yeah, everyone seems to have them, and they're all connected to the Internet."},{"start":272.83,"end":273.93,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Okay, good reason."},{"start":274.77,"end":277.37,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Now, how about this last one here?"},{"start":277.37,"end":283.25,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"The children's play area. Why did you put it second from bottom on the scale?"},{"start":284.15,"end":287.29,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"I guess because there are good and bad reasons for having one."},{"start":287.87,"end":293.49,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"If you're a parent, the good reason is a play area helps kids use up their energy."},{"start":294.41,"end":300.31,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Younger kids especially have so much energy, and it's better to use up some of it before they get on the plane."},{"start":300.31,"end":305.59,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"A reason not to have a play area is that, of course, kids can be noisy,"},{"start":305.97,"end":312.49,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"and the last thing other passengers want is a bunch of noisy kids playing while they're waiting to get on the plane."},{"start":312.97,"end":315.27,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"It just adds to the tension."},{"start":315.63,"end":318.17,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Okay. That's really helpful."},{"start":318.97,"end":323.91,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Now, there's just one more thing I'd like you to look at before we let you go."},{"start":324.39,"end":327.73,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"This is a floor plan of the new lounge area."},{"start":328.29,"end":336.41,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Now, thinking about what you've said already, where would you position the plants, the ferns, palms and things?"},{"start":336.91,"end":342.17,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Oh, without a doubt, in the middle. It would create a sort of avenue effect."},{"start":342.79,"end":344.83,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Yeah, right down the center there."},{"start":345.43,"end":348.51,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Okay. Chris, just write the letter A there."},{"start":349.17,"end":352.15,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"And I guess you'd put the toilets here, yes?"},{"start":352.63,"end":357.07,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Sure. Right by the gate. They should be the closest thing to the gate, in fact."},{"start":357.07,"end":359.27,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"There we go."},{"start":360.29,"end":362.67,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"And the coffee shop. Where would you put that?"},{"start":363.01,"end":369.81,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Again, very close to the gate. Somewhere convenient, like there, at the end of the walkway,"},{"start":370.19,"end":373.01,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"and with a window so you can see the view while you're drinking."},{"start":373.99,"end":376.39,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Let Chris just make a note of that."},{"start":377.82,"end":378.94,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"And what's this?"},{"start":379.82,"end":383.18,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Ah, sleeper chairs. You haven't mentioned those before."},{"start":383.18,"end":390.1,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Ah, they're a new kind of reclining chair, which allows you to sleep if you have a long wait ahead,"},{"start":390.46,"end":393.08,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"or you're transferring from another long flight."},{"start":393.52,"end":397.78,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"I see, erm, a sort of first-class lounge seat."},{"start":398.6,"end":402.54,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, I think the obvious place would be on the other side of the plants from the gate."},{"start":403.16,"end":407.14,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"You don't really want people staring at you sleeping while they're waiting."},{"start":407.86,"end":411.2,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"You've got lots of privacy here, and a window to look through too."},{"start":411.2,"end":414.62,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Good points. And now the last two things."},{"start":415.18,"end":419.94,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"I'm afraid the internet corner has already been confirmed as part of the plan,"},{"start":420.32,"end":425.46,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"so would you put it in the actual corner on the bottom to the right there?"},{"start":425.96,"end":430.46,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"No, I think that space would be better reserved for the play area."},{"start":431,"end":436.2,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"It's away from where most of the passengers sit, so they wouldn't be disturbed by the noise."},{"start":436.94,"end":440.42,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"The computer nerds can take the area next to it at the foot of the plan."},{"start":440.42,"end":441.88,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Serves them right."},{"start":442.86,"end":444.3,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Well, thank you so much."},{"start":444.72,"end":450.02,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"It's been fun talking to you, and I hope you find something to occupy yourself while you wait for your flight."},{"start":450.42,"end":453.18,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"No problem. I guess I'll just go and have another coffee."},{"start":454.18,"end":455.14,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Oh, one more thing."},{"start":455.5,"end":459.28,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Put your business card or your name and address in our lucky drawer hat,"},{"start":459.54,"end":463.14,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"and you could win a prize worth up to two thousand dollars."},{"start":463.46,"end":464.74,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"Okay, here goes."},{"start":465.28,"end":466.92,"speaker":"Airport lounge interview","text":"That's the end of task two."},{"start":467.3,"end":469.7,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."}],"3":[{"start":0,"end":63.81,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task three."},{"start":65.45,"end":72.45,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Linda has now invited a traveller to try some of the items available from the restaurants and coffee shops at the airport."},{"start":73.73,"end":76.21,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Put a take if the traveller likes the food."},{"start":77.16,"end":78.68,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"A cross if he doesn't."},{"start":79.28,"end":81.78,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Or a question mark if he's not sure."},{"start":83.29,"end":89.13,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"The items may not be mentioned in the same order as they appear in the question answer book."},{"start":90.07,"end":93.47,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"One space has been filled in for you as an example."},{"start":93.47,"end":97.66,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have thirty seconds to study the task."},{"start":98.69,"end":102.97,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"At the end of the task, you will have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":136.06,"end":144.48,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Hello, we're from the airport authority, and we're wondering if you'd like to try some of the food and drink items available at our various restaurant outlets."},{"start":145.26,"end":148.34,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Sure. I was just thinking how hungry I was."},{"start":148.88,"end":151.16,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Okay, let's start with the hot dog then."},{"start":151.76,"end":154.66,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Take a bite of that. It's from Hot Dog Express."},{"start":156.14,"end":161.22,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, I'm not a big hot dog fan, but I'll give it a go."},{"start":168.68,"end":171.89,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"No, I can't say this one persuades me either."},{"start":172.71,"end":175.41,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"No, that's not for me. It's too salty."},{"start":176.13,"end":179.47,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Make a note of that, Chris. Too salty."},{"start":180.9,"end":184.02,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Alright, perhaps you should choose something you like the look of."},{"start":185.16,"end":190.5,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, that tortilla looks pretty good. I love Mexican food usually."},{"start":194.06,"end":199.4,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Mmm, that's really good. And it's got loads in it."},{"start":199.74,"end":201.38,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"What's so special about it?"},{"start":202.67,"end":208.09,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, it's spicy. Really hot. And I don't mean heat hot."},{"start":209.17,"end":214.19,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"And the other thing is, it's really filling. You know, tortillas fill you up."},{"start":214.59,"end":218.29,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Not like some other snacks which just leave you feeling hungry."},{"start":218.29,"end":223.23,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Okay, that's from Viva Tortilla, which has only recently opened."},{"start":224.27,"end":227.49,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Now, what about these chicken skewers from the food court?"},{"start":228.05,"end":229.21,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"How do you feel about those?"},{"start":230.13,"end":232.25,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Let me just take one there."},{"start":235.77,"end":239.15,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Hmm. My sauce? Well, that's tasty."},{"start":240.06,"end":242.52,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Yeah, finger-licking good, as they say."},{"start":243.32,"end":246.22,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Just write down tasty sauce, Chris."},{"start":247.76,"end":251.08,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"The chicken's a bit stringy, though."},{"start":251.87,"end":256.48,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, very stringy. I could floss my teeth with that."},{"start":256.98,"end":258.98,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, what a horrible idea."},{"start":260.62,"end":265.14,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Stringy is just G-Y, Chris. Not G-E-Y."},{"start":265.8,"end":270.12,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, and I guess you should put a question mark in the second column."},{"start":271.04,"end":273.78,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"I'll have a word with the manager of the Sate House."},{"start":273.78,"end":277.36,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"In the meantime, perhaps you'd like to wash that down"},{"start":277.36,"end":281.02,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"with a sip of our tropical smoothie from the Waikiki bar."},{"start":285.67,"end":289.95,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Mmm, lovely. That hit the spot. It's very cool."},{"start":290.97,"end":293.19,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Icy cool, in fact, and refreshing."},{"start":294.4,"end":297.26,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Yeah, it really makes you feel refreshed."},{"start":298.26,"end":300.06,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, you've missed out on the sushi."},{"start":301.37,"end":303.97,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Actually, I was trying to avoid that."},{"start":304.87,"end":307.43,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Japanese isn't my favourite cuisine."},{"start":308.37,"end":309.57,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"I'll have a go, though."},{"start":312.34,"end":316.96,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, sorry. Do you have a napkin?"},{"start":318.28,"end":321.6,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Oh, that's not for me. It's much too fishy."},{"start":321.82,"end":323.72,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, it is raw fish."},{"start":324.54,"end":329.04,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Yes, I know. But there's fish, which I usually like,"},{"start":329.6,"end":334.81,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"especially with chips. Then there's, well, fishy, which I don't."},{"start":334.81,"end":339.87,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"How about a mouthful of cupcake to take the taste away?"},{"start":340.55,"end":341.61,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"I won't say no."},{"start":343.94,"end":344.5,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well?"},{"start":345.22,"end":349.02,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Mmm, just a minute. Mouthful."},{"start":350.87,"end":353.4,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, I can't decide, really."},{"start":354.3,"end":357.8,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"It's light. Not at all heavy, which is a good thing."},{"start":358.85,"end":360.67,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"But otherwise a bit tasteless."},{"start":361.27,"end":364.03,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Yeah, tasteless is the word I'd use."},{"start":364.61,"end":366.47,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Make a note of both of those, Chris."},{"start":366.47,"end":370.39,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"I can't make up my mind if I like it or not."},{"start":371.66,"end":374.68,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Well, thanks ever so much for helping us with the survey."},{"start":375.32,"end":380.12,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"Now, if you'd like to put your business card into our lucky drawer hat..."},{"start":380.12,"end":381.82,"speaker":"Traveller interview","text":"That's the end of task three."},{"start":382.28,"end":384.88,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have one minute to tidy up your answers."},{"start":447.88,"end":447.9,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task four."}],"4":[{"start":0,"end":0.52,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Task four."},{"start":1.47,"end":5.31,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"You are now attending a meeting of the research team with Linda"},{"start":5.31,"end":9.49,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and two other researchers called Simon and Sandy,"},{"start":9.49,"end":12.25,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"who are reporting on the survey results."},{"start":13.35,"end":17.55,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Based on what you hear in the conversation between Linda and the researchers,"},{"start":18.35,"end":23.05,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"fill in the spaces in the report below with details of the services"},{"start":23.05,"end":25.41,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and recommendations for improvements."},{"start":27.06,"end":30.24,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Remember to pay attention to spelling and grammar."},{"start":31.1,"end":34.54,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"One space has been filled in for you as an example."},{"start":35.42,"end":37.96,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have one minute to study the task."},{"start":37.96,"end":43.48,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"At the end of the task, you will have two minutes to tidy up your answers."},{"start":106.66,"end":110.5,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"All right, Chris, I've completed the framework of the report for you."},{"start":110.92,"end":112.72,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"You just have to fill in the details"},{"start":112.72,"end":118.16,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and remember to pay attention to grammar and spelling when you're doing that."},{"start":119.56,"end":123.68,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Simon has counted all our responses and come up with some percentage figures"},{"start":123.68,"end":125.42,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"along with travellers' comments."},{"start":126.14,"end":130.5,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"So how did the travellers rate our eating establishments, Simon?"},{"start":131.88,"end":132.88,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Pretty well, actually."},{"start":133.48,"end":136.46,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"About 60% said they found the services impressive."},{"start":137.24,"end":139.44,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, it's always good to impress people."},{"start":140.16,"end":142.98,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Then 15% weren't happy with the range."},{"start":143.56,"end":144.58,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"50%?"},{"start":145.06,"end":146.48,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"No, 15."},{"start":147.32,"end":149.8,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"And 25% hadn't used any restaurants,"},{"start":150.22,"end":152.48,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"so they couldn't say which ones they preferred."},{"start":152.48,"end":157.16,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Okay, don't bother writing about the 15%, Chris."},{"start":157.72,"end":160.1,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"We'll let people work that out for themselves."},{"start":161.55,"end":163.43,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"All right, let's move on to suggestions."},{"start":164.47,"end":167.99,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"How do people think our food choices can be improved?"},{"start":168.91,"end":172.83,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, first off, we should reduce the number of fast food outlets."},{"start":174.07,"end":179.49,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Less in the way of hamburgers, hot dogs, fried chicken and other salty snacks."},{"start":179.49,"end":183.91,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Yes, I have to agree. We do need to reduce them."},{"start":184.67,"end":188.19,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"There's too much emphasis on fast food. Go on."},{"start":189.39,"end":192.65,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Another request was to increase medium-priced restaurants."},{"start":193.63,"end":195.81,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Either you have very cheap fast food outlets"},{"start":195.81,"end":199.25,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"or upmarket eateries that are too pricey."},{"start":200.46,"end":203.88,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Increasing medium-priced restaurants would help balance things out."},{"start":204.6,"end":206.62,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Fair enough. That's worth noting down."},{"start":207.38,"end":211.74,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Finally, many felt we should provide a greater variety of food."},{"start":212.3,"end":215.42,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"And what did they mean by greater variety?"},{"start":215.72,"end":217.74,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, different cuisines, really."},{"start":218.56,"end":220.16,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Many wanted Japanese food."},{"start":220.78,"end":224.22,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"There is some available, but not really high-quality stuff."},{"start":225.2,"end":227.72,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"There were also a lot of requests for Indian food,"},{"start":228.06,"end":229.14,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and not just from Indians."},{"start":229.64,"end":232.24,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"The Japanese and the Singaporeans love curry,"},{"start":232.6,"end":233.94,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and so do many Westerners."},{"start":234.34,"end":235.44,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Any other requests?"},{"start":236.17,"end":239.24,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, there were a few for Middle Eastern food,"},{"start":239.62,"end":241.8,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"things like kebabs and falafels."},{"start":242.68,"end":245.32,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Middle Eastern food has a whole range of possibilities."},{"start":246.36,"end":246.78,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Interesting."},{"start":248.01,"end":250.59,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Okay, let's move on to other facilities now."},{"start":250.97,"end":253.71,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"What sort of requests did the travellers make, Sandy?"},{"start":254.43,"end":259.13,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, several people felt there should be more places of worship."},{"start":260.01,"end":261.15,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Places of worship?"},{"start":261.93,"end":264.61,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"You mean like chapels, that sort of thing."},{"start":264.61,"end":266.65,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"We already have one of those."},{"start":267.49,"end":271.05,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Yes, but we don't have a Muslim prayer room, for example."},{"start":271.59,"end":274.13,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Hmm, that's a bit of an oversight, really, isn't it?"},{"start":274.75,"end":275.85,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Write it down, Chris."},{"start":276.67,"end":282.03,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"You can spell Muslim either M-U-S-L-I-M"},{"start":282.03,"end":288.27,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"or M-O-S-L-E-M, your choice."},{"start":288.27,"end":294.37,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Oh, and prayer is spelt P-R-A-Y-E-R."},{"start":294.37,"end":294.97,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Got that?"},{"start":295.55,"end":298.43,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Any more places of worship to add, Sandy?"},{"start":299.25,"end":301.49,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, I'm not sure of discounts,"},{"start":301.81,"end":304.77,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"but someone suggested a meditation room."},{"start":305.31,"end":306.47,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"I like that idea."},{"start":307.33,"end":310.55,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Meditation's a good thing to do before you get on a plane,"},{"start":310.69,"end":313.79,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and it's not only Buddhists who like to do it."},{"start":314.01,"end":317.11,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"It's definitely worth including in the report."},{"start":317.79,"end":320.37,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"There were also a number of requests"},{"start":320.37,"end":322.51,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"for more entertainment facilities."},{"start":322.79,"end":323.57,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Such as?"},{"start":324.35,"end":326.87,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Well, I'm not sure if everyone would count"},{"start":326.87,"end":328.91,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"this as an entertainment facility,"},{"start":329.77,"end":333.21,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"but more than one person suggested a game centre."},{"start":333.69,"end":336.35,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Hmm, I don't think the airport authority"},{"start":336.35,"end":339.15,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"would be keen to give space to a game centre,"},{"start":339.75,"end":341.77,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"but I guess we ought to make a note of it."},{"start":342.19,"end":344.45,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Something they might be more happy to go for"},{"start":344.45,"end":345.79,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"is an art gallery."},{"start":345.89,"end":349.41,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Many travellers said they'd seen them in other airports"},{"start":349.41,"end":351.31,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and thought it was a great idea."},{"start":351.99,"end":352.95,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Yes, I can see why."},{"start":353.43,"end":356.31,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"There's something very relaxing about art galleries."},{"start":358.28,"end":361.1,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"OK, to sum up then, travellers at the airport"},{"start":361.1,"end":365.8,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"felt that the facilities provided were mostly satisfactory."},{"start":366.7,"end":368.5,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"I'd say that was about right, yes."},{"start":369.08,"end":373.08,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"So let's increase someone's level of satisfaction even more."},{"start":373.08,"end":377.42,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Would you like to pull the name out of the lucky drawer hat, Sandy?"},{"start":377.9,"end":379.06,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"OK, sure."},{"start":380.52,"end":384.68,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"Oh, it's Mr Pot of Jesterville, USA."},{"start":385.66,"end":389.32,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"His first name's not Jack by any chance, is it?"},{"start":389.42,"end":391.5,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"That's right. How did you know that?"},{"start":392.06,"end":393.8,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"That is the end of task four."},{"start":394.38,"end":397.64,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have two minutes to complete your answers to task four"},{"start":397.64,"end":400.14,"speaker":"Survey report meeting","text":"and to tidy up all your other answers."},{"start":400.14,"end":527.3,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Part B. Open your data file at page two."}]},"partB":[{"start":0,"end":0.05,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Part B. Open your data file at page two."},{"start":1.49,"end":3.9,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Situation. You are Marty Poon."},{"start":4.58,"end":7.2,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You work for a magazine called Asia Life."},{"start":7.96,"end":12.36,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You are an assistant to Casey Wong, the editor in charge of the magazine."},{"start":13.47,"end":17.69,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You will listen to a recording of a podcast called Travel Report."},{"start":18.79,"end":23.83,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"In the podcast, you will hear an interview with Adrian Lim and Kelly Johnson."},{"start":25.21,"end":29.53,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Before the recording is played, you will have five minutes to study"},{"start":29.53,"end":34.29,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"the question answer book and the data file for part B1"},{"start":34.29,"end":40.03,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and the question answer book and the data file for part B2."},{"start":41.2,"end":47.7,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Remember, you must choose to do the tasks in either part B1 or part B2."},{"start":48.18,"end":51.92,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Do not attempt both parts B1 and B2."},{"start":53.36,"end":56.76,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Complete the tasks by following the instructions"},{"start":56.76,"end":61.38,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"in the question answer book that you choose and on the recording."},{"start":62.34,"end":66.62,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You will find all the information you need in the question answer book"},{"start":66.62,"end":70.18,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and data file that you choose and on the recording."},{"start":71.18,"end":75.96,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"As you listen, you can make notes on page three of the data file."},{"start":77.88,"end":81,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"You now have five minutes to familiarize yourself"},{"start":81,"end":84.72,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"with the part B question answer book and the data file."},{"start":388.2,"end":389.96,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"The recording is about to begin."},{"start":390.82,"end":393.32,"speaker":"Narrator","text":"Turn to page three of the data file."},{"start":401.63,"end":403.83,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Welcome, everyone, to Travel Report."},{"start":404.77,"end":408.09,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"This is Scott Lamb bringing you this week's edition."},{"start":409.46,"end":413.22,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Let's welcome our guests for this week's podcast first of all."},{"start":414.32,"end":419,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I'm very pleased to have here in the pod tonight Adrian Lim."},{"start":419.9,"end":420.46,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Good evening."},{"start":420.87,"end":426.77,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Adrian, you're a travel agent specializing in unusual holidays."},{"start":427.45,"end":428.07,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Is that right?"},{"start":428.95,"end":430.57,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yes, that's right."},{"start":431.69,"end":436.11,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Okay, and we also have with us Dr. Kelly Johnson."},{"start":436.47,"end":436.73,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Evening."},{"start":438.82,"end":442.96,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Now, Kelly, you've been on the program lots of times before,"},{"start":443.36,"end":448.52,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"but just for those who don't know, you're a lecturer in travel and tourism."},{"start":448.98,"end":449.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, that's right."},{"start":451.06,"end":456.56,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Okay, let's begin this week then with the question, why do people travel?"},{"start":457.44,"end":457.7,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Adrian."},{"start":459.1,"end":464.22,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, I suppose people go on holiday and travel for many different reasons."},{"start":465.06,"end":465.72,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Such as?"},{"start":466.56,"end":471.58,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, a recent survey showed that the most popular reasons people gave"},{"start":471.58,"end":477.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"for going on holiday and traveling are wanting to challenge themselves and have fun."},{"start":477.8,"end":481.5,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, that's what I would have guessed people would say."},{"start":482.12,"end":486.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Sometimes we forget that having fun is as important as anything else."},{"start":487.7,"end":490.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, but people gave other reasons in the survey."},{"start":491.34,"end":492.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"They want to do other things."},{"start":493.24,"end":496.58,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"That's why they travel, like, say, learn a language."},{"start":497.3,"end":499.04,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"That's another reason to travel."},{"start":500.23,"end":501.29,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Like me, I guess."},{"start":502.07,"end":505.65,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I went to Japan after university to learn more Japanese."},{"start":505.65,"end":506.93,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Oh, so did I."},{"start":507.23,"end":510.25,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I'm not sure how much Japanese I learnt, though."},{"start":512.58,"end":514.76,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"So, that's a few reasons anyway."},{"start":515.88,"end":520.48,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"We travel to challenge ourselves, have fun, or learn a language."},{"start":522.06,"end":526.6,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"So, I suppose the reasons why people travel haven't changed much,"},{"start":527.18,"end":530.7,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"but other aspects of travel maybe have."},{"start":530.9,"end":531.84,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Mmm, that's right."},{"start":533.05,"end":537.51,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"So, what was different about travel, international travel, I mean,"},{"start":538.01,"end":541.87,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"in the past then, say, in the 1920s?"},{"start":542.31,"end":542.37,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Kelly?"},{"start":543.21,"end":549.05,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, the main differences about present-day travel compared to the 1920s,"},{"start":549.09,"end":552.75,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I suppose, if we're talking about international travel,"},{"start":553.21,"end":557.35,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"are things like the transport, how people traveled,"},{"start":557.67,"end":561.09,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and the length of time, I mean, how long it took."},{"start":561.96,"end":563.34,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"What was the transport?"},{"start":564.04,"end":566.06,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"By ship or train or...?"},{"start":566.06,"end":571.02,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, international travel meant people traveled by ship or by train."},{"start":572.34,"end":574.08,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, I was reading about this."},{"start":574.66,"end":578.2,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It took a long time, so that's why holidays were longer."},{"start":578.94,"end":583.84,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Like, it could take six weeks to travel by ship from London to Hong Kong for tourists."},{"start":584.5,"end":585.42,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Six weeks?"},{"start":585.96,"end":587.98,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Wow, can you imagine?"},{"start":588.74,"end":594,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Now, nowadays, it's really common for lots of people from all countries"},{"start":594,"end":595.74,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"to go abroad on holiday."},{"start":597.07,"end":600.27,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Was this always the case, or is this a recent phenomenon?"},{"start":601.38,"end":606.34,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I mean, was international travel an unusual holiday in itself in the past?"},{"start":607.12,"end":611.04,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, from my own research into this, yes, you're right."},{"start":611.68,"end":613.9,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It was only the very rich people."},{"start":613.9,"end":619.76,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Travel was very expensive, and, well, with the transport and time,"},{"start":620.34,"end":622.14,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"only rich people could do it."},{"start":622.93,"end":626.73,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"So, all of this holidays abroad is a new thing, then?"},{"start":626.99,"end":631.71,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, yes, it's really been in the last 30 years that it's really taken off."},{"start":632.98,"end":635.94,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"So, what's the most popular places to visit nowadays?"},{"start":636.96,"end":639.34,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Maybe Adrian, you'd be the person to ask."},{"start":639.8,"end":642.34,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Right, I've got some statistics here."},{"start":642.34,"end":643.96,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Let me see."},{"start":645.18,"end":649.08,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Last year, the most popular place to visit was India."},{"start":649.74,"end":651.82,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"76 million people went there."},{"start":652.36,"end":654.66,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"That's certainly different from 20 years ago."},{"start":655.64,"end":656.8,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"India. Okay."},{"start":657.88,"end":659.26,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Which other countries are popular?"},{"start":660.08,"end":662.92,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, the USA has lots of visitors."},{"start":663.66,"end":665.74,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"59 million went there last year."},{"start":666.36,"end":668.2,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Wow, 59 million."},{"start":668.98,"end":669.78,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"That's a lot."},{"start":669.78,"end":673.12,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yes, that's only slightly more than China."},{"start":673.88,"end":675.96,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"There were 55 million visitors."},{"start":677.32,"end":678.38,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"55 million."},{"start":679.36,"end":684.12,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I read, or maybe someone told me, that Spain is popular too."},{"start":684.8,"end":685.4,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Is that right?"},{"start":686.04,"end":688.5,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, Spain's still really popular."},{"start":689.06,"end":692.86,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It had about 52 million visitors last year, I think."},{"start":694.47,"end":698.89,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, I suppose all that tells us that more and more people are travelling."},{"start":698.89,"end":704.72,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"But I suppose the next thing is, what are they doing when they travel?"},{"start":706.31,"end":711.05,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, one thing I've noticed is that our customers want to stay in different places,"},{"start":711.87,"end":714.03,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"like these new types of unusual hotels."},{"start":714.63,"end":716.27,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Oh, that's interesting."},{"start":717.05,"end":720.71,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Can you give us an example of one of these unusual hotels?"},{"start":721.69,"end":724.25,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, the ICE hotels, they're popular."},{"start":725.48,"end":726.28,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"ICE hotels."},{"start":726.94,"end":728.06,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I've heard of them."},{"start":728.06,"end":731,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Is that like a hotel made of ice?"},{"start":732.68,"end":734.22,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Everything is made of ice."},{"start":734.78,"end":738.82,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"The rooms, the beds, tables, chairs, everything."},{"start":739.34,"end":741.26,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Our customers really love them."},{"start":741.84,"end":743.78,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I've always wondered, are they cold?"},{"start":744.36,"end":745.94,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"No, they aren't cold."},{"start":746.24,"end":747.82,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"But they are in cold countries."},{"start":748.7,"end":751.08,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I think I'd like to try staying in one."},{"start":751.93,"end":753.81,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Any more unusual hotels?"},{"start":753.81,"end":757.77,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Oh, I know. There's a prison hotel in Australia."},{"start":758.41,"end":759.87,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I stayed in it last year."},{"start":760.59,"end":761.75,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"A prison hotel?"},{"start":762.31,"end":766.49,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I thought you only stayed in a prison if you'd done something wrong."},{"start":767.39,"end":769.13,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, it's not any old prison."},{"start":769.75,"end":772.87,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"In Australia, some old prisons have closed,"},{"start":773.45,"end":775.29,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and then they've turned them into hotels."},{"start":775.95,"end":776.15,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Really?"},{"start":776.61,"end":780.27,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, you can sleep in a cell like a prisoner, but..."},{"start":780.27,"end":781.57,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"What, in a cell?"},{"start":782.17,"end":786.05,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You mean the hotel guests are locked up for the night in a prison cell?"},{"start":786.67,"end":788.63,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"No, you're not locked up."},{"start":789.07,"end":793.37,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"You sleep in a cell, but, I mean, you do have a key for your room."},{"start":793.81,"end":795.25,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It's really good fun."},{"start":795.65,"end":798.69,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Hmm, I'll have to take your word on that one, I think, Kelly."},{"start":800.11,"end":804.59,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, let's move swiftly on to maybe a more serious topic."},{"start":805.64,"end":808.42,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It certainly seems that more people are travelling,"},{"start":808.42,"end":811.92,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"but what are the effects on the countries they visit?"},{"start":813.15,"end":814.63,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"What about the local people?"},{"start":815.76,"end":819,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I mean, are there any negative effects from tourism?"},{"start":819.84,"end":823.5,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, yes, of course, there are always negative effects."},{"start":824.26,"end":828.32,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Some studies show that increased tourism brings increased crime."},{"start":829.34,"end":832.2,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Local people carrying out crimes against tourists."},{"start":833,"end":835.74,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"What kind of crimes? Serious or...?"},{"start":835.74,"end":841.82,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Things like stealing cameras or iPhones from tourists is very common,"},{"start":842.06,"end":844.9,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and they're relatively easy to steal."},{"start":845.78,"end":852.76,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"But I think it's important to emphasise that millions of tourists travel safely every year."},{"start":853.72,"end":855.08,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yes, I tend to agree."},{"start":855.78,"end":858.88,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"There are some very positive effects of tourism as well."},{"start":859.36,"end":860,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Such as?"},{"start":860.5,"end":862.78,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, of course, tourism brings in money."},{"start":863.42,"end":867.52,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yes, if we think about the number of people who are travelling,"},{"start":868.2,"end":871.36,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"lots more money is going to countries, and it comes from tourists."},{"start":872.68,"end":874.46,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"But what are the effects of money?"},{"start":875.18,"end":878.3,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, we can see the effects of money in countries"},{"start":878.3,"end":883.16,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"which can start to develop their infrastructure, and it's through..."},{"start":883.16,"end":888.18,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Sorry, what do you mean by developing an infrastructure in this context?"},{"start":888.66,"end":891.88,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Well, like building good roads and hospitals."},{"start":891.88,"end":893.82,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Everyone benefits."},{"start":894.92,"end":900.12,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Right. Building good roads and hospitals is obviously important, but..."},{"start":900.12,"end":906.5,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yes, and another positive effect of tourism is that countries maintain their traditions."},{"start":907.42,"end":912.22,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Some countries have kept up some of their customs because it brings in the tourists."},{"start":912.62,"end":914.1,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Yeah, I think this can be true."},{"start":914.82,"end":918.32,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I mean, like in Thailand, before international tourism,"},{"start":918.32,"end":922.54,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"some of the traditional dances, like the Nora Dance..."},{"start":922.54,"end":923.4,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"The what dance?"},{"start":923.82,"end":927.08,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"The Nora Dance. The name doesn't really matter."},{"start":927.42,"end":934.06,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"It's a traditional dance, and it had almost totally disappeared by the 1980s."},{"start":934.62,"end":939.9,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"But it's so spectacular that hotels started putting it on for all the tourists."},{"start":940.62,"end":945.4,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"And now there are Nora Dance festivals and competitions all over Thailand."},{"start":946.39,"end":949.55,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Right. Well, that's a positive way to end the program."},{"start":950.37,"end":954.85,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"I'd like to say a big thank you to our guests, Kelly and Adrian, this week,"},{"start":955.37,"end":957.31,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"and we'll see you all next week."},{"start":957.79,"end":958.17,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Bye."},{"start":977.34,"end":980.02,"speaker":"Travel Report guests","text":"Thank you."}]});})();
